course: dictionary
lesson: 10381
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word «tree» has more than one meaning. Its main meaning is a tall plant with a wooden trunk, branches and leaves. «Grey squirrels bury nuts in many separate spots, and the acorns they forget can grow into new oak trees.» Here, trees are plants that grow from acorns.
explain: «Tree» can also be part of a phrase with a different job. A family tree is a chart that shows a family's parents, children and grandparents. A tree diagram is a drawing with branches that shows choices or parts. The words around «tree» tell you which meaning to use.
explain: Use context to decide. Ask: what is being talked about? If it is growing in soil, it is the plant. If it is a family, a set of names or a set of choices, it is a chart or a drawing. «A boy in Vancouver looks out of the window at the far trees» clearly means real trees outside.
fact: «Tree» means a tall plant with a wooden trunk, branches and leaves.
fact: A family tree is a chart showing a family's parents, children and grandparents.
fact: A tree diagram is a drawing with branches that shows choices or parts.
fact: Phrases such as «climb a tree», «tree house» and «Christmas tree» help you see what «tree» means in use.
fact: The plural of «tree» is «trees».
exercise: «The grey squirrel buried its nut under the oak tree.» What does tree mean here? | A drawing with branches that shows choices | A chart showing a family's parents and children | *A tall plant with a wooden trunk, branches and leaves
exercise: Sam drew a family tree for his class project. What does tree mean here? | A drawing of a forest path | *A chart showing a family's parents, children and grandparents | A tall plant with leaves
exercise: Find the phrase that means a small house built up in a tree. | climb a tree | Christmas tree | *tree house | family tree
test: What is the plural of tree? | treess | tree's | treeing | *trees
test: In a tree diagram, what do the branches show? | *choices or parts | the weather for the week | the number of leaves on each plant
exam: Which meaning of «tree» fits this sentence: «Vervet monkeys run up trees when they hear the leopard call»? | A chart showing a family's parents and children | A drawing with branches that shows choices | *A tall plant with a wooden trunk, branches and leaves | A wooden table with four legs
